# NOTE: do not add `*.npz` here. `whest package` reads .gitignore and .whestignore as one
# pattern list with no `!` negation, so an ignored weights file is dropped from the
# submission tarball *silently* — the command still reports success, and the failure only
# surfaces on the grader as a setup() error that fails the whole submission. Shipping a
# weights.npz beside estimator.py is a documented, supported workflow
# (docs/how-to/ship-weights.md); nothing in this repo commits one, because
# examples/04_shipped_weights.py writes to a tempdir.

